problems.problem:
In the middle of the 17th century Christiaan Huygens was the first to measure the angular sizes of the discs of planets, in particular of Saturn. He also knew the orbital period of Saturn around the Sun and, of course, that the brightness of Saturn is about the same as that of bright stars. From this he managed to obtain an estimate of the distances to the nearest stars that was correct in order of magnitude (in astronomical units; the value of the astronomical unit itself was still known very poorly at that time).

Your task:

A) to reconstruct the information that Huygens knew;

B) to develop and describe the method of estimating the distances to stars used by Huygens;

C) to use the method and estimate the distance to the nearest stars;

D) to estimate the accuracy of the result that could have been obtained by this method in the middle of the 17th century.
